---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="What data Budget Home Fixes collects, which services process it, and how to control it.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: November 12, 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    Budget Home Fixes ("we", "us") publishes cost guides at thebudgethomefixes.com. This policy
    explains what happens to your data when you visit the site. You can reach us at
    <a href="mailto:hello@thebudgethomefixes.com">hello@thebudgethomefixes.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask you to create an account and we do not sell personal information.</li>
    <li>The site does not currently set cookies of its own, and it does not show advertising yet.</li>
    <li>We measure visits with a cookieless analytics service. Fonts and images are served from our own domain.</li>
    <li>If we turn on advertising, visitors in Europe will be asked for consent first.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <h3>Visit statistics</h3>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are useful. Cloudflare
    describes this product as not using cookies or other client-side storage and not fingerprinting
    individual visitors. It reports aggregate data such as pages viewed, referring site, country,
    browser, device type and page-load performance. We use it to improve the site, which is our
    legitimate interest.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting and delivery</h3>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, and our domain's DNS is managed by Cloudflare. Like any web
    host, these providers process technical request data such as your IP address and browser details
    to deliver pages and protect against abuse. We do not receive that data as personal information
    about you.
  </p>

  <h3>Email</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we use your address and message only to reply and to improve the guide you
    wrote about. Mail sent to our address is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to a Google
    Gmail inbox. We keep correspondence only as long as it is useful and delete it on request.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not currently set cookies of our own. The share links on article pages (X and Facebook) are
    ordinary links: they do not load those services' scripts, and nothing is shared with them unless
    you click. Once you are on a third-party site, its own privacy policy applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to show ads through Google AdSense. No ads or advertising cookies are active today. If we
    enable them, Google and its partners may use cookies and similar identifiers to serve and measure
    ads, and may personalize them based on your visits to this and other sites. For visitors in the
    European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, we will ask for your consent through a
    Google-certified consent management tool before any personalized advertising runs, and you will be
    able to change your choice later. Where US state privacy laws apply, we will provide the controls
    they require through Google's tools.
  </p>
  <p>You can already control personalized advertising across the web here:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> (US) and <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a> (Europe)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Affiliate and third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Some guides link to retailers, manufacturers or reference pages. We do not control those sites
    and are not responsible for their privacy practices. If we add affiliate links in the future, we
    will mark them clearly.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or UK GDPR), you may have the right to
    access, correct or delete personal data we hold about you, to object to processing, and to
    complain to your local data protection authority. Because we hold almost no personal data, the
    most common request is deleting an email conversation, and you can ask by writing to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a general audience resource for adults and is not directed at children under 16.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change, for example when advertising is switched on,
    and change the date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:hello@thebudgethomefixes.com">hello@thebudgethomefixes.com</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
